      "value": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948864/assets/6c52f315d079b82fb729c4ab47f210ec4bf2683d0dfe1adfe79c94db9fbc5f63.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows train routes between three stations, where nodes represent the stations and arrows represent the directed routes between them. The (incomplete) route matrix below represents information about the number of routes between each of the three stations. Find the value of $a+b+c.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">To:</td> \n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>A</b></td>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>B</b></td>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>C</b></td> \n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">From:</td>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$a$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$b$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$c$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
